{"text": "From: Gwendolyn Faulk <gfaulk@brassfieldfaulk.example>\nTo: \"Imanishi, Anselm\" <dr.imanishi@imanishiortho.example>\nCc: Keanu Kealoha <kkealoha@brassfieldfaulk.example>\nDate: Tue, 07 Jul 2026 16:42:10 -0700\nSubject: RE: Retention - Stojanovic v. Pendleton Regional Logistics (No. 34-2025-00381764) - PRIVILEGED\n\nAnselm,\n\nThank you for the call this morning. This confirms that Brassfield Faulk LLP is retaining you, through\nImanishi Orthopaedic Consulting, PLLC, as a testifying expert for the plaintiff in\nSTOJANOVIC v. PENDLETON REGIONAL LOGISTICS, INC., Superior Court of California, County of Sacramento,\nCase No. 34-2025-00381764. Please treat everything below as attorney work product.\n\n1. Scope. Review the records, examine Mr. Stojanovic once, and give opinions on causation, the\nreasonableness of past treatment, and future care. Short version of the facts: on October 3, 2024 a\nPendleton tractor backed into the loading dock where our client, Dragan Stojanovic (DOB 2/27/1979), was\nworking. He had an L4-L5 disc herniation with left-sided radiculopathy, failed conservative care, and\nunderwent a microdiscectomy on March 11, 2025 at Sutter Fork Spine Institute. He still has\nfoot drop on the left and takes gabapentin 600 mg three times a day. The defense will make a great\ndeal of a 2017 workers' comp claim for low back strain and of the fact that he was treated for alcohol dependence in 2021.\nYou should know both before you see their Rule 35 report.\n\n2. Rates. Per your fee schedule: $650/hour for review and conferences, $900 per hour for deposition and\ntrial testimony (four-hour minimum), exam flat fee $2,400. Travel at half rate.\n\n3. Retainer. We will wire $7,500.00 (seventy-five hundred dollars) this week against your first invoice. Per your W-9\n(EIN 84-3920175) and the wire sheet Keanu has:\n      Beneficiary:  Imanishi Orthopaedic Consulting, PLLC\n      Bank:         Osprey Delta Bank, Elk Grove branch\n      ABA:          116959977\n      Acct:         3300 7714 0926\n      Memo:         BF-24-1193 / Stojanovic\nKeanu will call your office manager at the number we have on file, 916-555-0156, to read the account back\nbefore anything is sent. We do not change wire details by email, ever.\n\n4. Records. About 2,100 pages, Bates STOJ-000001 through STOJ-002114, plus the MRI discs. They are on our\nshare: https://share.brassfieldfaulk.example/x/stoj-expert-7Qm4T9\nPassword (I'll also text it to you): Tulip!Harbor-2291\nThe link expires July 21. Please do not forward it to staff; if your assistant Meredith Oyelade needs\naccess, Keanu will set her up with her own login (moyelade-ext).\n\n5. Key dates. Expert disclosure 9/14/26. Your written report, if we decide we want one (think Fed. R.\nCiv. P. 26(a)(2)(B) format even though we are in state court), by August 28th. Depo window the weeks of\nOct. 5 and Oct. 12. Trial is set for January 11, 2027. Defense counsel is Hartsell Crane LLP.\n\n6. Exam. Mr. Stojanovic lives in Rancho Cordova and does not drive since the surgery; his wife Vesna will\nbring him. He is more comfortable in Serbian; tell us if you want an interpreter. He can do any\nweekday after the 20th. Her cell is (916) 555-0129.\n\nPlease countersign the attached engagement letter and send back the W-9 if the one we have (dated 2024) is stale.\nYou will be qualified under Cal. Evid. Code § 720 without any trouble.\n\nThanks,\nGwen\n\nGwendolyn R. Faulk | Partner | SBN 218846\nBrassfield Faulk LLP | 980 9th Street, Suite 1450, Sacramento, CA 95814\nDirect 916.555.0184 | gfaulk@brassfieldfaulk.example", "kind": "Email", "detail": "543 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Gwendolyn Faulk", "Imanishi", "Anselm", "Keanu Kealoha", "Dragan Stojanovic", "Meredith Oyelade", "Keanu", "Gwendolyn R. Faulk", "Mr. Stojanovic", "Vesna"], "companies": ["brassfieldfaulk", "Imanishiortho", "Stoller", "pendleton regional logistics", "Sutter Fork Spine Institute", "Brassfield Faulk LLP"]}, "topics": {"places": ["California", "Sacramento", "Rancho Cordova"], "health": ["disc herniation", "radiculopathy", "failed conservative care", "microdiscectomy", "foot drop", "gabapentin", "alcohol dependence", "workers' comp", "low back strain"], "sensitive": ["dob"], "names": ["Gwendolyn", "Anselm", "Keanu", "Dragan", "Imanishi", "Vesna", "Meredith"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.5, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "street", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "region", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 6, "end": 21, "text": "Gwendolyn Faulk", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Gwendolyn R. Faulk"}, {"start": 23, "end": 53, "text": "gfaulk@brassfieldfaulk.example", "kind": "email", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "gfaulk@brassfieldfaulk.example"}, {"start": 60, "end": 76, "text": "Imanishi, Anselm", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Anselm Imanishi"}, {"start": 79, "end": 112, "text": "dr.imanishi@imanishiortho.example", "kind": "email", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "dr.imanishi@imanishiortho.example"}, {"start": 118, "end": 131, "text": "Keanu Kealoha", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Keanu Kealoha"}, {"start": 133, "end": 165, "text": "kkealoha@brassfieldfaulk.example", "kind": "email", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "kkealoha@brassfieldfaulk.example"}, {"start": 173, "end": 198, "text": "Tue, 07 Jul 2026 16:42:10", "kind": "date", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "Tue, 07 Jul 2026 16:42:10"}, {"start": 230, "end": 240, "text": "Stojanovic", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Dragan Stojanovic"}, {"start": 244, "end":